<title>BELGIUM: Exceptionals boost GBL 1996 profits.</title>
<headline>Exceptionals boost GBL 1996 profits.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996.</p>
<p>(in billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net				 16.889 vs 6.602</p>
<p>    Net capital gains/exceptionals     9.898 vs 0.545</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)	     200    vs   195.33</p>
<p>NOTE: Groupe Bruxelles Lambert is Belgium's second biggest holding company.  </p>
<p>    Cons current profits		 7.763    vs  6.660</p>
<p>    Provisions/writeoffs		 0.026    vs  0.012</p>
<p>    Tax					0.022    vs  0.027</p>
<p>NOTE: GBL said the sale by Electrafina unit American Cometra of certain oil interests for $400 million would allow GBL to book a capital gain of two billion Belgian francs in 1997. This in turn would favourably influence the exceptional results in that year.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
